"Build a fully functional, scalable web application for a stickman MMORPG game using Node.js (server.js), WebSockets for real-time multiplayer, vanilla HTML/CSS/JS for the frontend, and minimal external libraries. Include the following features:

Core Requirements:

Real-time multiplayer with 100+ concurrent players visible on screen

2D top-down tile-based map (20x20 tiles initially, designed to scale to larger worlds)

Stickman characters with smooth movement (WASD/arrow keys), animations (idle, walk, attack)

Player authentication (simple username system, persistent across sessions)

Game World:

Small starter map with grass tiles, paths, trees, and 3 distinct areas (town, forest, dungeon entrance)

NPCs (3-5) with basic quest dialogue and markers above heads

2 simple quests: 'Talk to Village Elder' and 'Collect 5 sticks from forest'

Basic collision detection (walls, trees, other players)

Multiplayer Features:

Real-time player positions and animations synced via WebSockets

Player name tags and health bars

Proximity chat (players within 5 tiles can see messages)

Player list sidebar showing online players

Technical Architecture:

text
server.js (Node.js + Express + Socket.io)
├── Handles WebSocket connections
├── Player state management (positions, inventory, quests)
├── Basic zone instancing for scalability
├── Rate limiting and anti-cheat basics
└── REST API endpoints for static assets

public/
├── index.html (game canvas + UI)
├── game.js (main game loop, rendering, input)
├── player.js (stickman logic, animations)
├── map.js (tile rendering, collision)
├── websocket.js (real-time sync)
└── ui.js (HUD, inventory, chat)
Scalability Design:

Zone-based sharding system (players auto-move to adjacent zones)

Efficient delta-state updates (only send changes, not full state)

LOD (level of detail) for distant players

Configurable tile size and world chunk loading

Visual Style:

Clean stickman pixel art (simple lines, 32x32px sprites)

16x16px isometric tiles

Smooth 60fps gameplay

Minimalist UI with dark theme

Provide complete, production-ready code with:

Detailed comments explaining multiplayer sync logic

Error handling and reconnection logic

Responsive design (works on desktop/mobile)

Clear instructions for running locally

README with scalability roadmap (adding combat, items, larger maps)

Make it immediately playable with 2-3 sample accounts for testing multiplayer. Structure code modularly for easy expansion (combat system, inventory, more quests)."

